    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **283 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city title-casing on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the only endpoint that creates owners \u2014 the V2 controller only lists).\n\n**Change** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- In `addOwner`, before generating the customer code, the owner's city is now normalized via a new `normalizeCity(...)` step: `owner.setCity(normalizeCity(owner.getCity()))`.\n- `normalizeCity` scans existing owners; if one already lives in the same city (compared case-insensitively), it reuses that owner's **exact** existing spelling. Otherwise it title-cases the supplied city (`toTitleCase`), capitalizing the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lowercasing the rest (e.g. `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`), preserving original whitespace. Null cities pass through untouched (validation rejects empty cities separately).\n\nThe city returned in the `OwnerDto`'s `city` field is now the normalized value since it's set on the entity before mapping. The existing `customerCode` logic is unaffected \u2014 it uppercases the city, which is spelling-agnostic.\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`): added two cases \u2014\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCityForNewCity`: posts a lowercase multi-word city and asserts the response `city` is title-cased.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling`: creates an owner in a city, then creates a second owner submitting the city in all-caps, and asserts the response reuses the first owner's exact spelling.\n\nAll existing tests still pass (owner suite 29\u219231, full suite 283 green).",
